      "title": "SWK's Q3 Earnings Surge on Margin Expansion, 2026 Outlook Raised",
      "summary": "Stanley Black & Decker (SWK) reported Q3 adjusted earnings of $2.31 per share, up 61.5% year-over-year, driven by strong Tools & Outdoor segment performance and tariff refunds. The company raised its 2026 adjusted EPS guidance to $5.95-$6.25 and free cash flow forecast to $1.0-$1.2 billion. However, the Engineered Fastening segment faced headwinds with a 21% revenue decline due to the CAM divestiture and weaker automotive demand.",
